  "question": {
    "text": "Two spheres of equal masses but radii $r_1$ and $r_2$ are allowed to fall in a liquid of infinite column. The ratio of their terminal velocities is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$r_1: r_2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{r}_2: \\mathrm{r}_1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of the above",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have $\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\frac{2 r^2(\\sigma-\\rho) g}{9 \\eta}$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_1}{\\mathrm{v}_2}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{r}_1}{\\mathrm{r}_2}\\right)^2 \\frac{\\left(\\sigma_1-\\rho\\right)}{\\left(\\sigma_2-\\rho\\right)} ;$ given $\\mathrm{m}_1=\\mathrm{m}_2 \\Rightarrow\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{r}_1}{\\mathrm{r}_2}\\right)^3=\\frac{\\sigma_2}{\\sigma_1}$"
  }
}